course: dictionary
lesson: 8091
title: Remind: helping someone remember
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To remind someone is to help them remember something. «The sign of "The Red Lion" reminds him that he had not breakfasted that day.» The sign makes him think of food, so it reminds him of something he has forgotten: he has not eaten breakfast.
explain: Remind follows a pattern. You can remind someone to do something, remind someone about something, or remind someone of someone or something. Teachers often remind pupils about homework, kit and trips, and a reminder is the note or message that does the job.
explain: Something can also remind you of something else when the two are alike or connected. A smell or a song may remind a character of the past. Ask yourself: what does this make me think of? That is the clue to what remind means in the sentence.
fact: To remind someone means to help them remember.
fact: Remind is a verb: remind, reminds, reminded, reminding.
fact: A reminder is a note or message that helps someone remember.
fact: «Something reminds you of something» means it makes you think of it because they are alike or connected.
fact: A gentle reminder is often kinder than a telling-off.
exercise: «The tummy is zhyvIt, and at a sleepover his mum will remind you to "chystyty zUby", brush your teeth.» What does remind mean here? | To stop you from brushing your teeth | To buy you a new toothbrush | To wash your hair | *To help you remember to brush your teeth
exercise: «They gently remind your feet to keep away from the gap.» What does remind mean in this sentence? | To tread on the gap | *To help your feet remember to stay away from the gap | To cover the gap with laces | To forget the gap
exercise: Nadia says a reminder is just a telling-off. Is she right? | Yes, a reminder is always loud | *No, a gentle reminder is kinder than a telling-off | No, a reminder is only for teachers | Yes, they mean exactly the same
test: «I will give it back, Pau Amma, ... to remind you and all your children that I can make magics.» In this sentence, what does remind mean? | To ask you to be quiet | To make you forget something | To give you a present | *To make you remember something
test: A smell can remind a character of the past. What does remind mean here? | It makes the smell louder | It makes the character forget the past | *It makes the character think of something from before | It stops the smell
exam: Which pattern is correct for remind? | remind someone do something to | *remind someone to do something | remind something do someone | remind to someone do something
